-- title:
--   Level-automorphism translates of j are Gauss units
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and an integer $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Write $\overline{F}(M')$ for `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the full level-$M'$ modular function field $\mathbb Q(\mathrm{divisorExpansions}\,M')$, and $\overline{F}_{q,M'}$ for `fieldBar q M'`, the corresponding base change of the $X_H$-function field of level $q^2M'$ for $H=\ker\big((\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times\big)$; assume $\overline{F}(M')\subseteq\overline{F}_{q,M'}$. Let $\zeta$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, let $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, and let $O$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{F}_{q,M'}$ whose elements are exactly those $f$ admitting Laurent series $x,y$ with coefficients in $A$ such that $y$ has nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ and $f\cdot y=x$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ (the Gauss extension of $A$ at the cusp). Then for every $a\in A$ the element $\tau(j)-a$, where $\tau=\,$`levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` is the chosen $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-automorphism of $\overline{F}_{q,M'}$ attached to $(\zeta,\gamma)$ and $j\in\overline{F}(M')$ is the Laurent expansion `jq` of the modular invariant, lies in $O$ and is a unit of $O$.
--
--   This is the integrality-and-unit statement for the $q+1$ translates $j(q^2z)$, $j(z+b/q)$ of the modular invariant under the level automorphisms, read through the Gauss prolongation of a valuation ring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ to the Laurent series field at the cusp $\infty$. It feeds the identification of the maximal ideals occurring in the Igusa-ring descent arguments for the full-level model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_isUnit_levelAutBar_jBar_sub_algebraMap_of_gauss.lean

